cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Phantom transitions in phase-gated multi-agent voice systems"
abstract: >-
  A minimal reproduction, and fix, for a failure mode in phase-gated
  multi-agent voice systems. A real-time agent commits a phase-handoff tool
  call before the caller has finished speaking. The caller barges in, the
  speech and reasoning in flight are discarded, and the handoff is not, so the
  conversation advances to a stage the caller never triggered and no record
  distinguishes the two. Three fixes are given, and the tool-layer guard among
  them is established by twelve tests to have no bypass path reachable through
  the public API.
type: software
